statement:
For every P ∈ ℕ and every real σ > 0 there is a function ρ : ℝ^P → ℝ with all of the following properties:
- ρ is C^∞;
- ρ has compact support;
- ρ(y) ≥ 0 for every y;
- ρ(y) = 0 for every y with |y| ≥ σ;
- ∫_{ℝ^P} ρ dλ^P = 1.
Here λ^P is Lebesgue measure (`volume` on `Eucl P`) and |·| is the Euclidean norm.
